WEBVTT

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.080
The Enlightened One: Buddha.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.620
The Son of God: Jesus.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.740
Needless to say,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.170
they're the founders of Buddhism and Christianity, respectively.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.380
00:31-skip

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.890
Happy New Year

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.890
We'll be
reopening on
January 5th.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.890
The two of them

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.640
stayed together at a certain
apartment in Tachikawa City

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.900
Happy New Year

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.900
Matsuda
Heights

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.110
as they enjoyed a vacation

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.400
on Earth and celebrated

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:55.410
Saint

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.360
the coming of the new year.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.040
Um, excuse me. I'd like some Toppo.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.660
Oh, and some warm tea too.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.540
1:05-Various snacks, skip

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.540
Okay, your total is 400 yen.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.180
1:08-the priesthood

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.470
I'm sorry for paying with change.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.340
Not at all. This works fine.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.660
Excuse me.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.220
Thank you for your purchase.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.690
1:29-I entered the priesthood

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:34.370
Would anyone care for a boxed lunch, any snacks, or drinks?

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.710
My, this is wonderful.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.570
Oh, I'd like coffee.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:36.900
Right away!

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.160
Buddha, I figured you'd be against buying anything on the train.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.170
Well, it <i>is</i> expensive,

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.920
but I feel like we should make the most of this trip.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.770
Yeah.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.600
Traveling sure is nice.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.870
Sure is.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:06.060
2:03-Rurubu|Hakodate

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.060
Gosh, I'm so excited.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.200
I'm thinking of trying the crab once we reach Hakodate.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.410
Oh, but I guess something you can eat too would be better.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.440
It's okay. Don't mind me.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.360
Food aside, I'm looking forward to the Seikan Tunnel.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.200
Oh, the tunnel, huh?

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:30.320
Ah, but don't you feel a little nervous coming out of tunnels and such?

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.630
Oh? Do you usually try to hold your breath the whole time?

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:40.630
If I did that through the Seikan Tunnel, my stigmata would open up before the end.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.720
So, it's not that, but...

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.190
Say, which was the best?

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:56.280
I still wonder which expression would've been best to exit with after resurrecting, you see.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.280
You're really diligent when it comes to stuff like that, huh?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.490
Even idols and comedians don't want to mess up a return appearance, right?

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.020
Well, your image <i>is</i> important, after all.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:12.940
My centuries-old occupational sickness is a part of me now.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.180
Oh, what a blizzard!

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:21.020
Whoa! Everything's white.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.440
Gosh, the view from a train is the best, isn't it?

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:33.240
The view from a plane isn't much different from the view in Heaven, after all.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.520
Yeah, exactly!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:35.610
And...

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:55.040
I appreciate it, but it's pretty awkward.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.230
It makes you want to feign ignorance three times, like Peter.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.150
But hey, we don't have to worry about that on the train.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.230
Yeah.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.230
Wow!

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:09.100
As a matter of fact, here we are, traveling with our hearts at ea—

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:05.770
Awesome!

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:06.730
Awesome! Awe...

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.090
Hey, look out there!

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.600
It's dangerous, so sit down!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.140
We're flying through the sky!

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.140
...se?!

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.850
Awesome!

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:18.710
Huh?!

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.910
What?!

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.530
Welcome to Heaven
The land of Heaven is near

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.840
H-Hey... Why are we flying?

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.910
Weren't we on a bullet train to Hakodate?

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.190
Huh, what?

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:32.360
Did I cause some sort of miracle—

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.420
Whoa, amazing!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.760
We're really flying!

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.730
What is this? The Galactic Express?

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.620
H-Hey... E-Everyone, calm down.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.300
I-It's dangerous, so stay seated.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.810
Wait a second. Won't we be
forced back home at this rate?

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:48.950
Jeez!

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.000
I haven't bought Tokyo
Bananas to bring back ho...

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.690
I mean, wouldn't the other passengers get drag—

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.980
Calm down, Jesus.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.280
Buddha...

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.330
It's at times like these that we must not panic.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.070
Y-You're right.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.170
Me, of all people...

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:13.500
Here, use this to calm your nerves.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.920
Sorry, but <i>you</i> should calm down first.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.710
Y-You okay?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.590
And why a crab, anyway?

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.730
From your bag no less?!

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.150
What are you saying, Jesus?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.700
For those who are <i>taraba</i>led,

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.430
give them Taraba crab.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.540
"For those who are <i>taraba</i>led..."

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.200
Taraba crab sure is the thing!

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:57.210
5:49-Welcome

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.530
That's Punch of the comedy duo, Long-hair and Punch, for you!

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:56.210
For you to not lose sight of comedy even at a time like this...

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.990
Thank you, Buddha...

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.960
and Taraba cra—

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:06.840
Huh?

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.020
<i>Wh-Why?</i>

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.300
<i>In this situation, where no less than a Taraba crab would do...</i>

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.350
<i>Why?</i>

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:27.290
<i>Why is this feeling so unworthy of this great crab?</i>

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.410
<i>Just... why?</i>

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.310
For those...

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.680
For those who are <i>taraba</i>led...

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.710
What?!

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.360
Ow!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.750
How?!

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:19.390
S-Sorry!

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.750
D-Don't worry about it.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.860
Why?!

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.270
Just why?!

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:27.770
Huh?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.570
What? What's wrong?

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.700
I've died quite a few times already,

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:35.740
but my lives stay at "1"!

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.870
With this, I can just keep on playing, can't I?!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.450
Huh? What's wrong?

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.580
It's a nice freebie.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.310
That's not it!

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:48.110
Without having to insert additional coins...

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.370
A match that's played with just one coin...

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:55.760
I've heard that even arcade gamers wish to see the "No continue?" screen!

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.890
That sounds just like something a true gamer would say.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.160
H-Huh?

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.110
I-I see!

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.450
Huh?!

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.960
If my lives don't deplete,

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:13.900
I just have to start thinking there are no lives, correct?

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:15.780
Indeed.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.990
It's all like an internal struggle with Mara.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:22.090
Freed from the "samsara" of remaining lives,

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:25.430
we strive to achieve the "nirvana" of "No continue?".

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:26.730
Honestly, Buddha's really strong when he's cornered.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.730
Indeed!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:30.160
This is but the rugged path to attain enlightenment.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.500
Ta-da!

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.410
I-Isn't this bad?

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:40.890
Hey, Buddha!

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:43.720
Ping-pong!

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.650
I couldn't possibly attack them...

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.780
Wh-What are we going to do?!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.080
O-Oh, right!

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.860
Your lives won't deplete.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:02.420
B-But that means we'll never see the "No continue?" sign!

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:05.540
Even so, we can't clear the level like this!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:10.920
To think I was the one who learned how to attain enlightenment to escape samsara...

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.640
Space, star!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.950
How can we not even escape this game?!

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.360
Yum, yuck.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.940
Heh, take that!

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.960
Bang, hi-yah!

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:33.750
Na...

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.060
Namusen!

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:44.140
Ta... Taraba!

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.920
No continue...

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:54.620
Huh?

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.970
No continue...

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.630
Huh?

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.630
No con...

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:02.780
No continue...

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:03.640
It's said that

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.690
on the next morning, anything involving

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.860
No continue...

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:14.130
their first dreams of the year on Earth was left unsaid.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:15.250
No continue...

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:18.070
No con...

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.680
No con...

00:12:40.230 --> 00:14:09.320
CM - "Sho-Gyo-Mujyo" by Ryomei Shirai. 諸行無常 = "All worldly things are transitory" or "The impermanence of worldly things"

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:11.120
Oh, Buddha!

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.240
It's that commercial from before.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.090
First of its kind in all of human history.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.760
God Vacation the Animation...

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:22.690
H-Huh?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:24.070
is finally here.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.330
This narration...

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.470
Isn't the genre a little off?

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:28.890
Huh?

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:29.590
Oh...

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:33.800
That's the commercial Bonten made for us.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.270
Asura was driven to tears!

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:39.210
An emotional film comparable to the apocalypse!

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:40.940
Say, Buddha...

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.190
Is this really okay to use?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.780
Saint☆Young Men: The Movie.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.160
Bonten, we appreciate the effort,

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.100
but I see you're just doing your own thing as usual.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.360
Honestly, his enthusiasm got the better of him.
